    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of all changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### CLI Changes (`frai-cli/src/index.ts`)\n- Added `threshold?: string[]` to `EvalOptions` interface\n- Created `parseThresholds()` function that validates:\n  - Format: `<metric>=<number>`\n  - Values are between 0 and 1\n  - Metric IDs exist (exits with code 2 for invalid input)\n- Updated `runEvalCommand()` to extract metric IDs, parse thresholds, and pass them to `generateReport`\n- Added `--threshold` option to the eval command (can be used multiple times)\n- CLI exits with code 1 if any threshold fails\n\n### Core Logic (`frai-core/src/eval/index.js`)\n- Added optional `thresholds` parameter to `generateReport()`\n- Added logic to check each threshold against metric scores\n- Metrics with `null` scores fail their thresholds\n- Report includes `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` array with results for each threshold\n- Threshold results include: metric id, minimum value, actual score, and pass/fail status\n\n### Reporting (`frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`)\n- Updated markdown reporter to include \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n- Section only appears if thresholds were checked\n\n### Tests (`frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`)\nAdded 6 new tests covering:\n- Passing thresholds\n- Failing thresholds\n- Metrics with no score\n- Multiple thresholds\n- Markdown output with thresholds\n\n### Documentation (`README.md`)\nUpdated the `frai eval` command reference with the new `--threshold` option\n\n**Key Features:**\n- \u2705 Multiple thresholds via repeated `--threshold` flags\n- \u2705 Exit code 1 on threshold failure, 0 on success\n- \u2705 Exit code 2 for malformed thresholds or unknown metrics\n- \u2705 Reports always written, regardless of threshold result\n- \u2705 Backward compatible\u2014no changes when `--threshold` not used\n- \u2705 Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`",
